SUSPECTED BUG (precision): errors.Join(Refund(n), Void(n)) guarded by if errors.Is(err, ErrInternal) { return nil }.
Whenever either operand is ErrInternal the join matches and nil is returned, so ErrInternal must NOT appear.
Actual: ErrInternal is kept, marked possibly handled "wrapped value may be nil" - but an operand that is nil
is not ErrInternal either. The rest is as expected: ErrDeclined (via Refund's inner join and via Void) and
ErrDuplicate stay under errors.Join chains.
